IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg9-x-sale-of-assets`
IMPORT `dg9-x-dissolution`
IMPORT `dg9-x-winding-up`
IMPORT `dg9-xi-receivers`
IMPORT `dg9-xii-revival`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 (sections 101 to 398), the text of 2026-10-01 -- piece dg9, LAYER 2:
-- THE SEAT LAYER for Subchapter X (sale of assets, dissolution and winding up), Subchapter XI (insolvency; receivers
-- and trustees) and Subchapter XII (renewal, revival, extension and restoration of the certificate of incorporation).
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law:
-- an incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder. They ask what the Law lets
-- them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
-- There is never a seat for an official: the Secretary of State, the Court of Chancery, the Register in Chancery, the
-- Attorney General, a receiver or trustee and the bankruptcy court appear only as what the person is owed or exposed to.
--
-- Nothing here is new law. Every question below is the question of a person in the seat about a rule already encoded in
-- the five layer-1 modules imported above; it takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one for
-- each fact that person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked, builds the layer-1 inputs in
-- its WHERE, and calls the layer-1 rule. No rule is restated or copied, and no layer-1 module changes to suit this one.
--
-- A fact that layer 1 takes as a MAYBE (a date that may not exist) is asked as a yes/no and a date, the date being ignored
-- when the answer is No. A party that layer 1 takes as an Actor is asked as yes/no answers about the person's role.
-- An answer of NOTHING (a MAYBE result) means the text does not answer that case.
--
-- Facts the text hands to someone else are asked as facts and are never guessed: that the corporation is insolvent, that
-- stockholders are unable to agree, that a person shows good cause, that the board deems a sale expedient, what the Court
-- of Chancery directs or deems necessary. Facts that are other pieces' outputs are asked as facts: execution, filing and
-- effectiveness under section 103, notice under section 222, consent under section 228. Chapter 5 of the Law (franchise
-- taxes), Title 6, the Federal Bankruptcy Code and the Rules of the Court of Chancery are not among the inputs: what
-- depends on them is a plain fact or figure. Where the Law lets the certificate of incorporation or a court vary a rule,
-- the question asks for the variation.
--
-- Questions are grouped under § headings in the text's order. Where a group arises only in a situation the person may not
-- be in, the heading's comment says so, so that a form can ask "Has this happened to you?" before showing the group.

§ `Delaware General Corporation Law, Subchapters X to XII -- the questions of an incorporator, director, officer or stockholder`

§§ `Selling, leasing or exchanging the corporation's assets; mortgages and pledges (ss 271, 272)`

-- Only if the corporation proposes to sell, lease or exchange its property and assets, or to mortgage or pledge them.

-- Section 271(a) needs a resolution for all or substantially all of the assets (counting the subsidiaries', 271(c)); a sale to a wholly-owned, controlled subsidiary needs none unless the certificate of incorporation says so.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a), (c)
@export Must the stockholders vote on our sale, lease or exchange of the corporation's property and assets (s 271(a), (c))?
GIVEN `the sale, lease or exchange covers all or substantially all of the property and assets of the corporation, counting those of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the sale, lease or exchange cover all or substantially all of your corporation's property and assets, counting those of its subsidiaries?
      `the transferee is wholly-owned by the corporation, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the buyer, lessee or other party to the exchange wholly-owned by your corporation, directly or indirectly?
      `the transferee is controlled by the corporation, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that party controlled by your corporation, directly or indirectly?
      `our certificate of incorporation requires a resolution for a sale, lease or exchange to a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation require a stockholder resolution even for a sale, lease or exchange to a subsidiary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 271(a) the stockholders must vote on our sale, lease or exchange of assets` IS
    `s 271(a) and (c) a resolution of the stockholders or members is required for the sale, lease or exchange` WITH `the sale, lease or exchange covers all or substantially all of the property and assets of the corporation, counting those of its subsidiaries` IS `the sale, lease or exchange covers all or substantially all of the property and assets of the corporation, counting those of its subsidiaries`, `the transferee is a subsidiary of the corporation` IS (`s 271(c) the entity is a subsidiary of the corporation` WITH `the entity is wholly-owned by the corporation, directly or indirectly` IS `the transferee is wholly-owned by the corporation, directly or indirectly`, `the entity is controlled by the corporation, directly or indirectly` IS `the transferee is controlled by the corporation, directly or indirectly`), `where a provision requiring a resolution for a sale, lease or exchange to a subsidiary is made` IS (IF `our certificate of incorporation requires a resolution for a sale, lease or exchange to a subsidiary` THEN `in the certificate of incorporation` ELSE `in none of these`)

-- A majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote (a stock corporation), or of the members entitled to vote (a nonstock corporation), at a meeting duly called upon at least 20 days' notice that states the resolution will be considered.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(a)
@export Was our sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all of the corporation's assets validly authorized by the board and the stockholders (s 271(a))?
GIVEN `our corporation is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a nonstock corporation (one with members, not stockholders)?
      `the board of directors or governing body acted at a meeting and deems the terms and the consideration expedient and for the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At a meeting, did the board of directors or governing body decide that the terms and the consideration are expedient and for the best interests of the corporation?
      `the votes in favor of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favor of the resolution (votes, not people: a share with more or fewer than one vote counts that many)?
      `the votes entitled to be cast on the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were entitled to be cast on it (all the outstanding stock entitled to vote, or all the members entitled to vote)?
      `the meeting was duly called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting of stockholders or members duly called (sections 211 and 222)?
      `the date notice of the meeting was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was notice of the meeting given? (a date such as 2026-03-01)
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the meeting held?
      `the notice stated that such a resolution will be considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice of the meeting state that such a resolution would be considered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 271(a) our sale, lease or exchange of assets is validly authorized` IS
    `s 271(a) the sale, lease or exchange is authorized` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS (IF `our corporation is a nonstock corporation` THEN `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` ELSE `a stock corporation`), `the board of directors or governing body acted at a meeting and deems the terms and the consideration expedient and for the best interests of the corporation` IS `the board of directors or governing body acted at a meeting and deems the terms and the consideration expedient and for the best interests of the corporation`, `the votes in favor of the resolution` IS `the votes in favor of the resolution`, `the votes entitled to be cast on the resolution` IS `the votes entitled to be cast on the resolution`, `the meeting was duly called` IS `the meeting was duly called`, `the date notice of the meeting was given` IS `the date notice of the meeting was given`, `the date of the meeting` IS `the date of the meeting`, `the notice stated that such a resolution will be considered` IS `the notice stated that such a resolution will be considered`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(b)
@export May the board abandon the sale, lease or exchange without a further vote of the stockholders after they approved it (s 271(b))?
GIVEN `the stockholders or members have authorized or consented to the proposed sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the stockholders or members authorized or consented to the proposed sale, lease or exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 271(b) the board may abandon the sale, lease or exchange that the stockholders approved` IS
    `s 271(b) the board or governing body may abandon the proposed sale, lease or exchange without further action by the stockholders or members` WITH `the stockholders or members have authorized or consented to the proposed sale, lease or exchange` IS `the stockholders or members have authorized or consented to the proposed sale, lease or exchange`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(b)
@export If the board abandons the sale, lease or exchange, do third parties keep their rights under a contract relating to it (s 271(b))?
GIVEN `a third party has rights under a contract relating to the proposed sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a third party have rights under a contract relating to the proposed sale, lease or exchange?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 271(b) a third party's contract rights survive our abandoning the sale, lease or exchange` IS
    `s 271(b) the third party's contract rights survive the abandonment` WITH `a third party has rights under a contract relating to the proposed sale, lease or exchange` IS `a third party has rights under a contract relating to the proposed sale, lease or exchange`

-- For purposes of section 271 only, the property and assets of the corporation include those of its subsidiaries; whether the sale is of 'all or substantially all' of that total is for the caller to say.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 271(c)
@export What is the value of the corporation's property and assets for section 271, counting those of its subsidiaries (s 271(c))?
GIVEN `the value of the property and assets of the corporation itself` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the corporation's own property and assets, in dollars?
      `the value of the property and assets of all the subsidiaries of the corporation together` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the property and assets of all of its subsidiaries together, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 271(c) the value of our property and assets, counting our subsidiaries'` IS
    `s 271(c) the value of the property and assets of the corporation, counting its subsidiaries'` WITH `the value of the property and assets of the corporation itself` IS `the value of the property and assets of the corporation itself`, `the values of the property and assets of each subsidiary of the corporation` IS (LIST `the value of the property and assets of all the subsidiaries of the corporation together`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(a)
@export Must the stockholders authorize or consent to a mortgage or pledge of the corporation's property and assets (s 272(a))?
GIVEN `our certificate of incorporation requires the authorization or consent of stockholders to a mortgage or pledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation require stockholder authorization or consent to a mortgage or pledge of the corporation's property and assets?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 272(a) the stockholders must consent to a mortgage or pledge of our assets` IS
    `s 272(a) the authorization or consent of stockholders to the mortgage or pledge is necessary` WITH `where a provision requiring the authorization or consent of stockholders to a mortgage or pledge is made` IS (IF `our certificate of incorporation requires the authorization or consent of stockholders to a mortgage or pledge` THEN `in the certificate of incorporation` ELSE `in none of these`)

-- No resolution is required by section 271(a) for collateral the secured party sells itself (b)(1), or that the board sells instead to reduce the secured debt where the value is no more than the debt and the law governing the mortgage does not forbid it (b)(2).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(b)
@export Do the stockholders not need to vote under section 271(a) because the assets are collateral that the secured party is selling or the board is selling to reduce the debt (s 272(b))?
GIVEN `the property or assets are collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the property or assets collateral that secures a mortgage, or pledged to a secured party?
      `the secured party exercises its rights under the law governing the mortgage or pledge to effect the sale, lease or exchange without the consent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the secured party itself exercising its rights under the law governing the mortgage or pledge (for example Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code) to effect the sale, lease or exchange without the corporation's consent?
      `the board of directors authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange, whether with the secured party or with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Instead, has the board authorized an alternative sale, lease or exchange, with the secured party or another person?
      `the alternative sale, lease or exchange results in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by the property or assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the alternative result in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by the property or assets?
      `the value of the property or assets` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the property or assets, in dollars?
      `the total amount of the liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of the liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced, in dollars?
      `the sale, lease or exchange is prohibited by the law governing the mortgage or pledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law governing the mortgage or pledge prohibit the sale, lease or exchange?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 272(b) the stockholders need not vote on the sale of our collateral` IS
    `s 272(b) no resolution by stockholders is required by s 271(a) for the sale, lease or exchange of the collateral` WITH `the property or assets are collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party` IS `the property or assets are collateral that secures a mortgage or are pledged to a secured party`, `the secured party exercises its rights under the law governing the mortgage or pledge to effect the sale, lease or exchange without the consent of the corporation` IS `the secured party exercises its rights under the law governing the mortgage or pledge to effect the sale, lease or exchange without the consent of the corporation`, `the board's alternative sale, lease or exchange qualifies under s 272(b)(2)` IS (`s 272(b)(2) the board's alternative sale, lease or exchange qualifies` WITH `the board of directors authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange, whether with the secured party or with another person` IS `the board of directors authorizes an alternative sale, lease or exchange, whether with the secured party or with another person`, `the alternative sale, lease or exchange results in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by the property or assets` IS `the alternative sale, lease or exchange results in the reduction or elimination of the total liabilities or obligations secured by the property or assets`, `the value of the property or assets` IS `the value of the property or assets`, `the total amount of the liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced` IS `the total amount of the liabilities or obligations being eliminated or reduced`, `the sale, lease or exchange is prohibited by the law governing the mortgage or pledge` IS `the sale, lease or exchange is prohibited by the law governing the mortgage or pledge`)

-- The protection does not reach a proceeding to enjoin the transaction before it is completed. FALSE says only that this protection does not apply, not that the transaction is invalid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(c)
@export If the value test of section 272(b)(2)(i) was not met, does the sale, lease or exchange still stand (s 272(c))?
GIVEN `the transferee provided value for the property or assets, which may include the reduction or elimination of the liabilities or obligations secured by them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the transferee give value for the property or assets (this may include reducing or eliminating the secured liabilities)?
      `the transferee acted in good faith as defined in § 1-201(b) of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the transferee act in good faith, as section 1-201(b) of Title 6 defines it?
      `the proceeding is one against the corporation and any other necessary parties to enjoin the sale, lease or exchange before its consummation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking a court, before the sale, lease or exchange is completed, to enjoin it in a proceeding against the corporation and the other necessary parties?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 272(c) the transferee's purchase stands although the value test failed` IS
    `s 272(c) the failure to satisfy the proviso in s 272(b)(2)(i) does not invalidate the sale, lease or exchange` WITH `the transferee provided value for the property or assets, which may include the reduction or elimination of the liabilities or obligations secured by them` IS `the transferee provided value for the property or assets, which may include the reduction or elimination of the liabilities or obligations secured by them`, `the transferee acted in good faith as defined in § 1-201(b) of Title 6` IS `the transferee acted in good faith as defined in § 1-201(b) of Title 6`, `the proceeding is one against the corporation and any other necessary parties to enjoin the sale, lease or exchange before its consummation` IS `the proceeding is one against the corporation and any other necessary parties to enjoin the sale, lease or exchange before its consummation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(c)
@export Can a claim for damages for breach of fiduciary duty about the sale, lease or exchange still be brought against a current or former director, officer or stockholder (s 272(c))?
GIVEN `the claim is based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim based on a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director, officer or stockholder (including a claim in the right of the corporation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 272(c) I can still be made to pay damages for a breach of fiduciary duty about the sale` IS
    `s 272(c) liability for monetary damages for the claim is not eliminated by the protection of the transferee` WITH `the claim is based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder` IS `the claim is based upon a violation of fiduciary duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder`

-- Subsection (d) reaches only certificate provisions that first became effective on or after 1 August 2023; for an earlier one the subsection says nothing.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 272(d)
@export Does a provision of our certificate of incorporation requiring stockholder consent to a sale also apply to a sale of collateral permitted by section 272(b) (s 272(d))?
GIVEN `the date the certificate provision first became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the certificate provision requiring stockholder authorization or consent first become effective?
      `the certificate provision expressly requires its application to a transaction permitted by s 272(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision expressly say that it applies to a transaction permitted by section 272(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 272(d) our certificate's consent requirement applies to a collateral sale` IS
    `s 272(d) the certificate provision requiring stockholder authorization or consent applies to the transaction permitted by s 272(b)` WITH `the date the certificate provision first became effective` IS `the date the certificate provision first became effective`, `the certificate provision expressly requires its application to a transaction permitted by s 272(b)` IS `the certificate provision expressly requires its application to a transaction permitted by s 272(b)`

§§ `Dissolving the corporation (ss 273 to 277)`

-- Only if the corporation is being dissolved, or has a joint venture of two stockholders that is deadlocked, or has not yet issued shares or begun business.

@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(a)
@export As one of two 50% stockholders in a joint venture corporation who cannot agree, may I file a petition with the Court of Chancery to discontinue the venture or dissolve the corporation (s 273(a))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a corporation of this State (Delaware)?
      `the number of stockholders` IS A NUMBER @desc How many stockholders does the corporation have?
      `the proportion of the stock owned by the petitioner` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the stock do you own? (0.5 for half)
      `the proportion of the stock owned by the other stockholder` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the stock does the other stockholder own? (0.5 for half)
      `the stockholders are engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the two stockholders engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture?
      `the stockholders are unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the stockholders unable to agree on discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it?
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide otherwise (that is, forbid or replace this petition)?
      `a written agreement between the stockholders provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written agreement between the stockholders provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 273(a) I may petition the Court of Chancery to wind up our two-stockholder joint venture` IS
    `s 273(a) either stockholder may file a petition with the Court of Chancery` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS `the corporation is a corporation of this State`, `the number of stockholders` IS `the number of stockholders`, `the proportion of the stock owned by the petitioner` IS `the proportion of the stock owned by the petitioner`, `the proportion of the stock owned by the other stockholder` IS `the proportion of the stock owned by the other stockholder`, `the stockholders are engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture` IS `the stockholders are engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture`, `the stockholders are unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it` IS `the stockholders are unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it`, `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`, `a written agreement between the stockholders provides otherwise` IS `a written agreement between the stockholders provides otherwise`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(a)
@export Is my petition to wind up the joint venture in order, with the plan and the certificate attached and executed under section 103 (s 273(a))?
GIVEN `the petition states that the stockholder desires to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or, if no plan is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the petition state that you desire to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan both stockholders agree, or, if none is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved?
      `a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution attached?
      `a certificate is attached stating that copies of the petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate attached stating that copies of the petition and plan were sent in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers?
      `the petition and the certificate were executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the petition and the certificate executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 273(a) my petition for the joint venture is in order` IS
    `s 273(a) the petition is in order` WITH `the petition states that the stockholder desires to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or, if no plan is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved` IS `the petition states that the stockholder desires to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or, if no plan is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved`, `a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution is attached` IS `a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution is attached`, `a certificate is attached stating that copies of the petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers` IS `a certificate is attached stating that copies of the petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers`, `the petition and the certificate were executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103` IS `the petition and the certificate were executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103`

-- The Court may act when either certificate is missing once its period (3 months, 1 year, as extended by a certificate filed before it ran out) has passed. The Court 'may': this says only that the text puts it in a position to.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(b)
@export Has the time run out so that the Court of Chancery may now dissolve our joint-venture corporation and appoint trustees or receivers (s 273(b))?
GIVEN `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the petition filed with the Court of Chancery?
      `the date of the question` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (or the date you are asking about)?
      `both stockholders filed the certificate that they have agreed on the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have both stockholders filed with the Court the certificate that they agreed on a plan?
      `the date both stockholders filed the certificate that they have agreed on the plan` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it filed? (ignored if No)
      `both stockholders filed the certificate that the distribution is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have both stockholders filed with the Court the certificate that the distribution under the plan is completed?
      `the date both stockholders filed the certificate that the distribution is completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it filed? (ignored if No)
      `we extended the 3-month period by a certificate filed with the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree to extend the 3-month period, by a certificate filed with the Court?
      `the date to which we extended the 3-month period` IS A DATE @desc To what date did you extend it? (ignored if No)
      `the date we filed the certificate extending the 3-month period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file that certificate? (ignored if No)
      `we extended the 1-year period by a certificate filed with the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree to extend the 1-year period, by a certificate filed with the Court?
      `the date to which we extended the 1-year period` IS A DATE @desc To what date did you extend it? (ignored if No)
      `the date we filed the certificate extending the 1-year period` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file that certificate? (ignored if No)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 273(b) the Court of Chancery can now dissolve our joint-venture corporation` IS
    `s 273(b) the Court of Chancery may dissolve the corporation and appoint trustees or receivers to administer and wind up its affairs` WITH `the date of the question` IS `the date of the question`, `the last day of the 3-month period, as extended` IS `the last day of the 3 months`, `the last day of the 1-year period, as extended` IS `the last day of the 1 year`, `the first certificate was filed within its period` IS (`s 273(b) the stockholders' certificate was filed within the period` WITH `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did` IS (IF `both stockholders filed the certificate that they have agreed on the plan` THEN JUST `the date both stockholders filed the certificate that they have agreed on the plan` ELSE NOTHING), `the last day of the period, as extended` IS `the last day of the 3 months`), `the second certificate was filed within its period` IS (`s 273(b) the stockholders' certificate was filed within the period` WITH `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did` IS (IF `both stockholders filed the certificate that the distribution is completed` THEN JUST `the date both stockholders filed the certificate that the distribution is completed` ELSE NOTHING), `the last day of the period, as extended` IS `the last day of the 1 year`)
    WHERE
        `the last day of the 3 months` MEANS `s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery`, `the period` IS `period in months` 3, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS (IF `we extended the 3-month period by a certificate filed with the Court` THEN JUST (`s 273(b) Extension of a period` WITH `the date to which the period is extended` IS `the date to which we extended the 3-month period`, `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS `the date we filed the certificate extending the 3-month period`) ELSE NOTHING)
        `the last day of the 1 year` MEANS `s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery`, `the period` IS `period in years` 1, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS (IF `we extended the 1-year period by a certificate filed with the Court` THEN JUST (`s 273(b) Extension of a period` WITH `the date to which the period is extended` IS `the date to which we extended the 1-year period`, `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS `the date we filed the certificate extending the 1-year period`) ELSE NOTHING)

-- Only a charitable nonstock corporation owes the copy; for any other kind there is nothing to comply with, so the answer is Yes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(c)
@export If our corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation, have I given the Attorney General a copy of my petition within a week of filing it (s 273(c))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation.
      `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the petition filed with the Court of Chancery?
      `I gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Attorney General of Delaware a copy of the petition?
      `the date I gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (ignored if No)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 273(c) I have given the Attorney General the copy of my petition in time` IS
    `s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `the kind of corporation`, `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery`, `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS (IF `I gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition` THEN JUST `the date I gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition` ELSE NOTHING)

-- A majority of the directors if directors were named or elected, otherwise a majority of the incorporators; and only if the corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced business.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 274
@export May a majority of the incorporators or directors surrender the corporation's rights and franchises by certificate because it has not issued shares or begun business (s 274)?
GIVEN `the corporation has issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued shares?
      `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation commenced the business for which it was organized?
      `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were directors named in the certificate of incorporation, or have directors been elected?
