-- Two routes: the board's resolution by a majority of the whole board at a meeting called for the purpose, notice to the stockholders, and a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote; or the written consent of all the stockholders entitled to vote.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(a), (b), (c)
@export Is the dissolution of our corporation authorized, by the board and a majority of the stockholders, or by the written consent of all the stockholders (s 275(a), (b), (c))?
GIVEN `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors voted for the resolution to dissolve?
      `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors make up the whole board?
