GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 277 we may dissolve, merge, transfer or convert the corporation` IS
    `s 277 the corporation may be dissolved, merged, transferred or converted` WITH `all franchise taxes due or assessable, including those for the entire calendar month in which the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion becomes effective, have been paid by the corporation` IS `all franchise taxes due or assessable, including those for the entire calendar month in which the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion becomes effective, have been paid by the corporation`, `all annual franchise tax reports, including a final report for the year in which it becomes effective, have been filed by the corporation` IS `all annual franchise tax reports, including a final report for the year in which it becomes effective, have been filed by the corporation`, `the Secretary of State certifies that an instrument to effect the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion has been filed` IS `the Secretary of State certifies that an instrument to effect the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion has been filed`

§§ `Winding up after dissolution: continuation, notice to claimants, distribution and liability (ss 278 to 285)`

-- Only after the corporation has been dissolved, has expired by its own limitation or has had its charter revoked or forfeited.

@ref 8 Del. C. § 278
@export Until what day does our dissolved corporation continue as a body corporate, 3 years from its dissolution or the longer period the Court of Chancery directed (s 278)?
GIVEN `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation expire by its own limitation or get dissolved?
      `the Court of Chancery has directed that the corporation be continued for a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery directed that the corporation be continued for a longer period than 3 years?
      `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued` IS A DATE @desc If so, to what date? (ignored if No)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 278 the last day our dissolved corporation continues as a body corporate` IS
    `s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved`, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS (IF `the Court of Chancery has directed that the corporation be continued for a longer period` THEN JUST `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued` ELSE NOTHING)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 278
@export May our dissolved corporation, on this date, still act as a body corporate for this purpose (s 278)?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 278 Purpose for which a corporation continues` @desc For what purpose would the corporation act? One of: prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against the corporation; enabling the corporation gradually to settle and close its business; disposing of and conveying its property; discharging its liabilities; distributing to its stockholders any remaining assets; continuing the business for which the corporation was organized.
      `the date of the question` IS A DATE @desc On what date would it act?
      `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation expire by its own limitation or get dissolved?
      `the Court of Chancery has directed that the corporation be continued for a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery directed that the corporation be continued for a longer period than 3 years?
      `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued` IS A DATE @desc If so, to what date? (ignored if No)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 278 our dissolved corporation may still act for this purpose` IS
    `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `the purpose`, `the date of the question` IS `the date of the question`, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS `our last day of continuation`
    WHERE
        `our last day of continuation` MEANS `s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved`, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS (IF `the Court of Chancery has directed that the corporation be continued for a longer period` THEN JUST `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued` ELSE NOTHING)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 278
@export Does a suit begun by or against our corporation before, or within 3 years after, its dissolution carry on, solely for the suit, until the judgment is fully executed (s 278)?
GIVEN `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the suit begun by or against the corporation before, or within 3 years after, its expiration or dissolution?
      `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the judgments, orders or decrees in the suit been fully executed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 278 a suit about our dissolved corporation does not abate` IS
    `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate, and the action does not abate, for the sake of the action, suit or proceeding` WITH `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution` IS `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution`, `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed` IS `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 278
@export Do sections 279 to 282 (trustees, notice to claimants, distribution, stockholder liability) apply to our corporation (s 278)?
