§§ `Insolvency, receivers and trustees, and bankruptcy (ss 291 to 303)`

-- Only if the corporation is insolvent, has a receiver or trustee, or is in a proceeding under the Federal Bankruptcy Code.

-- Only a creditor or a stockholder may apply under section 291. A director who is neither may not, unlike the application for a dissolved corporation under section 279.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 291
@export May I apply to the Court of Chancery to appoint receivers for our insolvent corporation, as a creditor or a stockholder (s 291)?
GIVEN `the corporation is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation insolvent?
      `I am a creditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a creditor of the corporation?
      `I am a stockholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of the corporation?
      `I am a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 291 I may apply for a receiver for the insolvent corporation` IS
    `s 291 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint receivers for the insolvent corporation` WITH `the corporation is insolvent` IS `the corporation is insolvent`, `the applicant` IS `me as applicant`
    WHERE
        `me as applicant` MEANS IF `I am a creditor of the corporation` THEN `a creditor` ELSE IF `I am a stockholder of the corporation` THEN `a stockholder` ELSE IF `I am a director of the corporation` THEN `a director` ELSE `another party named in the provision` "a person who is none of these"

@ref 8 Del. C. § 291
